  "note": "A salient is own ground projecting toward the En, an enclave for him (MW s9 para 2 a p 124); it radiates threats on several axes and leaves little room to deploy (p 126). Its defence (MW s14 pp 178-179): the outer periphery, the central arch, held lightly with strong dispositions on the shoulders; key features as Pl / Coy strong points with the bias toward the shoulders (para 1 a); the depth localities prepared for occupation by the reserves at short notice, some partly occupied from the outset (para 1 b), drawn planned (dashed) here; the reserves central, quick to reinforce or recapture on interior lines (para 1 f, h), split per sub-sector where the tracks are poor (para 2 d). The Left and Right Bns hold the shoulders, B Coy of the third Bn the arch as Pl strong points, the rest of that Bn the Bde reserve in the centre. A Bn guards one major approach in an important sub-sector, wider frontages with wide gaps elsewhere (para 1 g); the arch takes more troops than a linear border and is fired on from three sides, and the En's envelopment is aimed at its base (para 2 a-c). Laid square to the threat on the Bde row (OoW Vol I Annexes B-D, a yardstick; MW prints no figure, frontages large in mountains, MW p 148). The shoulders face out as well as forward: turn their localities on the ground.",
